💭 A function that returns its own parameter.
💭
💭 Expected: the program prints "done" and nothing else.
💭 What happens: see README.md. ↩️ value, where value is a parameter, returns it without
💭 retaining it, and the caller releases what it got as if it had been retained. With a
💭 temporary as the argument the text is freed while the caller still holds it, and the
💭 next text that is made takes its place.
💭
💭 Copying the parameter into a variable first is fine: value ➡️ kept, then ↩️ kept.
